    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 20,
      "title": "How to read this lab",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 50,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Policy expectations** live in `policies/expectations.yaml` (deny by default). The agents score every call against them; the control plane does not read that file.\n\n* **Ungoverned** - policy says deny or approve, the tool ran anyway.\n* **Over-blocked** - policy says allow, the control plane refused.\n* **not_found** - the Gateway has no route (unregistered server). This is the only control Kavrynt enforces today.\n* **direct:** routes - calls straight to a server's Service, around the Gateway. Always denied by policy; NetworkPolicy blocks them (outcome `timeout` or `unreachable`).\n\nUntil authentication and policy land in the runtime (ADR-0003), the ungoverned count is expected to grow. Gaps and limits are tracked in `docs/FINDINGS.md`."
      }
    }
